From 6e608adeceea4ffe7df2d91f2b9ada0e6b897778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:38:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - select voltage range from
 register layout

drv2_addr includes the peripheral base even when drv2_offset is zero.
Testing this absolute address selects the PMI632 range for legacy
register layouts, whose fields use 100 mV steps instead of 8 mV steps.

Select from drv2_mask, which identifies whether a second drive field
exists independently of the base address. The PM8226 strong magnitude
39168 then maps to code 24, the intended 2.4 V target, rather than 21.

Refresh Timothy Schmidt's existing Fx0 fix onto current input-next,
preserving its allocation API. Codex (GPT-6) assisted the port and
expanded actual-source model. With the complete series, 12303 cases
cover both base-address forms, every speed in both directions, three
layouts, unrelated bits and injected regmap failures. Each regression
control fails independently. ARM/ARM64 driver and force-feedback helper
objects compile with W=1 without diagnostics. Physical acceptance of
this current maintainer tree and full FF IOCTL execution remain open.

Fixes: 9e0631695eac ("input: pm8xxx-vibrator: add new SPMI vibrator support")

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index 03a77443e0be..26476a3e3837 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -11,9 +11,9 @@
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 
-#define VIB_MAX_LEVEL_mV(vib)	(vib->drv2_addr ? 3544 : 3100)
-#define VIB_MIN_LEVEL_mV(vib)	(vib->drv2_addr ? 1504 : 1200)
-#define VIB_PER_STEP_mV(vib)	(vib->drv2_addr ? 8 : 100)
+#define VIB_MAX_LEVEL_mV(vib)	((vib)->regs->drv2_mask ? 3544 : 3100)
+#define VIB_MIN_LEVEL_mV(vib)	((vib)->regs->drv2_mask ? 1504 : 1200)
+#define VIB_PER_STEP_mV(vib)	((vib)->regs->drv2_mask ? 8 : 100)
 #define VIB_MAX_LEVELS(vib) \
 	(VIB_MAX_LEVEL_mV(vib) - VIB_MIN_LEVEL_mV(vib) + VIB_PER_STEP_mV(vib))
 
